; The compiler's test programs banked on Wendy 2 run with `--disk DIR` (lathe/env/wendy2disk.env):
; placement D of lathe/docs/configurations.md for the modules that exist, and the small build's
; tables (SMALL 1), because there is no data bank yet: every table is in fixed memory,
; $0200-$7FFF and $F810-$FFF9, beside the resident code. src_support.build_program(...,
; banked=True) builds with it and runs on the wendy2disk board (lathe/host/README.md, "The
; banked build"); configurations.md, "Measured on the compiler's test programs", has the numbers.
;
; Fixed: err, kernel, src, lex, typetab, fold, fbuf, sys and the run-time modules (disk,
; rt_bank, rt_math, rt_frame). Bank 2, code generation: gen, reg, out; and cond in bank 3, which
; is placement E, D's fallback: with cond, bank 2 is judged 1,437 bytes over 28 KB in gentest
; (the linker judges a bank as written, before zero page shrinks it: configurations.md, "As
; built"), though it would hold 26,000 bytes as placed. Bank 1, the front
; end: until lathec, decl and expr exist it holds the test drivers, script, listing, regcmd and
; the test's main module, which stand where the front end will stand: above code generation,
; calling down into it and into fixed memory, called by nothing below. The harness adds the
; main module's `place` line, and drops those of modules a program does not link (an unlinked
; placed module is link error 44).
;
; The fixed code ends at $7FFF and starts where the variables end; the split is set by gentest,
; the largest (lathe/host/README.md, "The banked build").
cpu       65c02
zeropage  $00 $FF
code      $3A00 $7FFF
data      $0200 $39FF
more      data $F810 $FFF9
stack     $FF
exit      stop
output    raw
window    WIN $8000 $EFFF
switch    WIN bank $F000 $1F
bank      WIN 1 $11 LATHE1.BIN
bank      WIN 2 $12 LATHE2.BIN
bank      WIN 3 $13 LATHE3.BIN
place     script WIN 1
place     listing WIN 1
place     regcmd WIN 1
place     gen WIN 2
place     reg WIN 2
place     cond WIN 3     ; placement E: D does not fit (below)
place     out WIN 2
farcall   rt_bank
define    BOARD 2
define    DISK 1
define    PORTS 1     ; sys over the file ports (lathe/rt/disk.lth)
define    SMALL 1     ; the tables at the small build's sizes
